---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
import SectionHeading from '../components/SectionHeading.astro';
import { sourceLinks } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Game"
  description="Explore The Stars Don’t Wait’s player fantasy, core loops, living galaxy, and explicit first-release scope."
>
  <PageIntro
    eyebrow="Game / Design direction"
    title="Make a life between the stars."
    intro="The Stars Don’t Wait is a single-player 3D space sandbox in development: a long journey from one modest ship to wealth, reputation, and influence inside a galaxy that continues without you."
  >
    <div class="button-row">
      <a class="button-secondary" href={sourceLinks.gameDesign}
        >Full game design document <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a
      >
    </div>
  </PageIntro>

  <section class="container section-pad game-status">
    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        <strong
          >The current build is a substantial playable slice, not a finished
          game.</strong
        >
        Flight, combat, the persistent galaxy and economy, outfitting, factions, missions,
        the opening campaign act, exploration, mining, salvage, custom UI, navigation,
        targeting, and rebindable controls are implemented and verified. Content breadth,
        audio, deeper faction territory changes, a cockpit-integrated HUD, and performance
        hardening remain ahead.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-pad">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Four pillars"
      title="The rules that hold the fantasy together."
    />
    <div class="pillar-grid">
      <article class="pillar panel">
        <span>01</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Pilot, not cursor</h3>
          <p>
            Experience the world from a ship you directly fly. The map informs
            the journey; it does not replace the cockpit.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar panel">
        <span>02</span>
        <div>
          <h3>A universe in motion</h3>
          <p>
            Traders, pirates, and factions pursue their own goals. The player
            enters an existing system instead of triggering it into life.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar panel">
        <span>03</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Nobody to somebody</h3>
          <p>
            Power is earned through ships, equipment, knowledge, money, and
            relationships—not character levels.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
      <article class="pillar panel">
        <span>04</span>
        <div>
          <h3>Systems over scripts</h3>
          <p>
            Data-driven content and sandboxed Lua scripting let the base game
            use the same layering mechanisms as mods.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wide-container section-pad loops-section">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Core loops / Committed design"
      title="A reason to care at every scale."
      intro="Each layer should work on its own, from the feel of one maneuver to the consequences of a long career."
    />
    <ol class="loop-list">
      <li>
        <div class="loop-time">Moment</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Fly the ship</h3>
          <p>Maneuver, manage momentum, fight, dodge, dock, and scan.</p>
        </div>
        <span class="confidence-chip">Core</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="loop-time">30–90 min</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Make a run</h3>
          <p>
            Follow a contract, trade route, signal, asteroid field, wreck, or
            unexplored gate—then return to sell, refine, and refit.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="confidence-chip">Core</span>
      </li>
      <li>
        <div class="loop-time">Tens of hours</div>
        <div>
          <h3>Shape a career</h3>
          <p>
            Build standing, find enemies, acquire specialized ships, open new
            markets, and eventually seed wider influence.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="confidence-chip likely">Likely</span>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-pad world-section">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">The galaxy / Committed design</p>
      <h2>Procedural breadth. Authored character.</h2>
      <p class="world-copy">
        The design targets a seeded network of 50–150 systems, organized into a
        civilized core, contested frontier, and lawless fringe. Faction
        identities, ships, economy rules, and story anchors are handcrafted;
        generation decides how they inhabit the galaxy.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="world-facts panel">
      <ul class="fact-list">
        <li>
          <strong>Gate lanes + cruise</strong>
          Travel remains at 1× real time, with distances and cruise speeds tuned for
          short, consequential legs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Persistent state</strong>
          Markets, faction relations, mission progress, survey knowledge, depletion,
          wrecks, fleet state, and fittings survive in one continuous save.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Local information</strong>
          Markets respond to station stock. Remote reports age, so travel and renewed
          observation still matter.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container section-pad">
    <SectionHeading
      eyebrow="Scope guardrails"
      title="A focused space game, by design."
      intro="These are explicit non-goals for the first shipped version, not missing promises."
    />
    <ul class="scope-list scope-grid">
      <li><strong>Not included:</strong> multiplayer of any kind</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not included:</strong> planetary landings or atmospheric flight
      </li>
      <li><strong>Not included:</strong> walking aboard ships or stations</li>
      <li><strong>Not included:</strong> block-based ship construction</li>
      <li><strong>Not included:</strong> colony-scale empire management</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Not included:</strong> huge fleet battles, VR, or base building
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .game-status {
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .pillar-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .pillar {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: auto 1fr;
    padding: var(--space-6);
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  .pillar > span {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--2);
  }

  .pillar p {
    margin: var(--space-3) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .loops-section {
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
  }

  .loop-list {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .loop-list li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 9rem 1fr auto;
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    gap: var(--space-6);
  }

  .loop-time {
    color: var(--color-accent-bright);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: var(--step--1);
  }

  .loop-list p {
    margin: var(--space-2) 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .world-section {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 0.85fr;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-8);
  }

  .world-copy {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
  }

  .world-facts {
    padding: var(--space-5) var(--space-6);
  }

  .scope-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    border-block: 1px solid var(--color-line);
    column-gap: var(--space-7);
  }

  .scope-grid strong {
    color: var(--color-warm);
  }

  @media (max-width: 54rem) {
    .pillar-grid,
    .world-section,
    .scope-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .loop-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr auto;
    }

    .loop-time {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 34rem) {
    .loop-list li {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
